      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7p",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1778342856,
      "version": 562,
      "versionNonce": 385324185,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1780048478634,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Worker thread wrapper:\n1.) execute payload\n2.) decrement counter\n3.) remove waiting fibre from wait list if the counter is zero (from the wait list of the counter to the threads local queue)\n    - (naughty dog engine allows waiting for arbitrary counter values, not just zero, I can't see why this would be needed)\n4.) fibre context switch back to the scheduler fibre ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Worker thread wrapper:\n1.) execute payload\n2.) decrement counter\n3.) remove waiting fibre from wait list if the counter is zero (from the wait list of the counter to the threads local queue)\n    - (naughty dog engine allows waiting for arbitrary counter values, not just zero, I can't see why this would be needed)\n4.) fibre context switch back to the scheduler fibre ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
